0.19.3
• Prevented invalid recovery copies and copies made before legacy cleanup from retrying whenever the Shopping List window opens.

0.19.2
• Added list cost projections showing spending, remaining target cost, projected total, current and planned budget balances, and entries without maximum prices.
• Added optional local price suggestions from Tamriel Trade Centre, EsoHub, Master Merchant, and Arkadius Trade Tools for linked items.
• Added explicit Use Suggestion actions for keyboard and gamepad editors without replacing or saving the player's chosen maximum price automatically.

0.19.1
• Removed duplicate lists created by the retired legacy recovery, including saves where some copies had already been deleted manually.
• Made the Getting Started and Release Notes content scrollable so longer text is no longer cut off.

0.19.0
• Allocated backpack, bank, and craft bag stock once across matching Own Total entries in active shopping trips, with specific matching rules receiving stock first.
• Added purchase corrections for acquired quantities, reductions, unit prices, incorrect history records, and undoing the latest matched transaction.
• Added automatic safety copies before purchase corrections.
• Added persistent list locking while keeping searching, sharing, session viewing, and automatic purchase tracking available.
• Added Find Next for the current item view and an optional setting that selects the next needed entry after a matched purchase.
• Added current guild store result markers for Shopping List matches, price targets, completion, and specific matching rules in the standard store and AwesomeGuildStore.

0.18.8
• Added a shopping session summary for matched purchases, actual spending, updated lists, and live remaining entry counts.
• Expanded the public API to manage, inspect, select, reorder, archive, restore, duplicate, delete, and reset shopping lists.
• Added live remaining quantity snapshots and non-mutating matching previews that use purchase allocation order.
• Added protected list, item, and purchase update callbacks for companion addons while retaining API v1 and v2 compatibility.
• Added atomic crafting material transfers for companion addons, defaulting to merged Own Total targets so live inventory determines what remains.
• Added optional WritWorthy integration to send a Master Writ's required materials to the current list from its right click menu.

0.18.7
• Reorganized runtime code into Core, Features, Integrations, and shared, keyboard, and gamepad UI modules without changing saved variable identities.
• Added per list item searching plus sorting by name, quantity, owned quantity, completion, price target, and date added in keyboard and gamepad interfaces.
• Added persistent favorite and pinned lists plus optional list categories; pinned lists appear first while preserving manual list order.

0.18.5
• Added duplicate detection for keyboard, gamepad, linked item, and bulk adds with Merge, Replace, and Keep Separate choices.
• Duplicate comparisons respect item identity, matching rules, and Buy More versus Own Total target modes; batch choices commit atomically.
• Reset Progress now clears purchased and manual completion quantities only, preserving list contents, notes, rules, budgets, purchase history, and recorded spending.
• Added per item Buy More and Own Total quantity targets in the keyboard and gamepad editors.
• Own Total entries now calculate remaining quantity and completion from matching backpack, bank, subscriber bank, and craft bag inventory without recording owned items as purchases.
• Added deactivation and logout checkpoints while retaining ten distinct recovery states without filling the history with identical copies.
• Separated full guild store transaction spending from the cost allocated to quantities that shopping list entries actually needed; list budgets now use full transaction spending.
• Added backup size and health reporting before SLB1 codes approach their hard limit.
• Cleared retained AwesomeGuildStore filters before Shopping List searches, including name only searches.
• Centralized matching rules, quantities, prices, item counts, names, notes, and link limits across data, editors, sharing, backup validation, bulk entry, and the public API.

0.18.0
• Added LibSets backed set searching to item autocomplete.
• Added actual tradeable set pieces for crafted and bind on equip sets while excluding bind on pickup gear from guild store suggestions.
• Kept ESO's trading house name results as a fallback alongside set searching.

0.17.0
• Expanded the public API with atomic named list creation and batch item addition.
• Added optional set, trait, quality, level, and Champion Point matching overrides for integrations.
• Added explicit list name conflict handling, stable API v2 errors, and failing item indexes.
• Added checksummed SL2 sharing for item links, notes, matching rules, and price targets while retaining SL1 imports.
• Kept API v1 item addition and active list discovery compatible.

0.16.4
• Added complete Spanish and French localizations with English fallback.
• Corrected localization files not loading because ESO manifests do not expand wildcard paths.
• Kept the main list selector label independent from the item filter dropdown.
• Prevented runtime only SavedVariables metadata from invalidating full backup generation.

0.16.3
• Added a versioned public API that allows other add ons to add linked or name only items to active shopping lists.
• Added safe list discovery, current list defaults, optional notes, and stable API error codes.
• Added developer integration documentation and ESOUI ready BBCode examples.
• Distinguished same named weapon, armor, and jewelry traits in item editor dropdowns.
• Renamed the manifest and Lua namespaces to GravvyShoppingList to avoid Master Merchant's legacy ShoppingList importer warning.

0.16.2
• Added an option to add linked chat items to the current shopping list from their right click menu.

0.16.1
• Restored the Trait, Quality Rule, Quality, and Level Rule dropdowns in the keyboard item editor.
• Corrected Craft Bag quantities by enumerating virtual bag slots with their sparse slot IDs.

0.16.0
• Added live owned quantities from the backpack, bank, subscriber bank, and craft bag without changing purchase progress.
• Added persistent notes for lists and individual items.
• Added full data SLB1 backup and restore codes while keeping lightweight SL1 list sharing codes unchanged.
• Added font scaling, stronger contrast, and optional non color only status indicators.
• Added keyboard and gamepad workflows for notes and full data backup and restore.

0.15.4
• Completed gamepad list management with create, rename, duplicate, delete, reorder, budget, and clear completed actions.
• Added persistent Undo for deleted items, deleted lists, and batches cleared with Clear Completed.
• Added bulk item entry with support for pasted item and quantity lines.
• Added All, Needed, Completed, Over Price Target, and Rule Restricted item filters.
• Added optional merged shopping trips across selected active lists while keeping inactive lists untouched.
• Kept the mouse cursor active after closing the item removal confirmation while the shopping list remains open.
• Corrected the Active Shopping Lists description layout so the full text wraps inside the window.
• Restored the shopping list cursor when returning to ESO after switching to another application.

0.15.3
• Minor bug fixes and improvements.

0.15.2
• Added an in game chat warning that names any required libraries that are missing.

0.15.1
• Lists can now be archived whether they are unfinished, completed, or empty.
• Corrected the Archive button appearing unresponsive for unfinished lists.

0.15.0
• Added in game help and recent release notes for keyboard and gamepad.
• Added the /shoppinglisthelp command and a ? button in the main window.

0.14.0
• Added the gamepad Manage menu.
• Added controller editing for matching rules and price targets.
• Added controller archive, restore, share, and import workflows.

0.13.6
• Corrected Import dialog layering above the Share window.

0.13.5
• Added the optional NA only in game donation mail shortcut.

0.13.4
